    "body": "1. It seems fine to switch to \"with\" there.\n2. I'm not sure I understand this. [Code points](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-points) is our recommendation for how to represent code points in documents, but here we are not trying to represent a code point. We are using a literal syntax to represent a [list](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list). If we used the syntax for code points it would not be understood as a list. I'm also not sure I share the general concern as often you do something with the list that makes it clear that it is a list to the reader and the reader only has to pick this up once and after that can apply this knowledge to many specifications.",
