    "updated_at": "2026-06-08T13:50:23Z",
    "body": "I was unclear.\n\nMy suggestion would be to change the above-quoted paragraph to the following, which uses the W3C i18n-WG-recommended template, and which could be copied-and-pasted into a PR:\n```\n <p>For notational convenience, a literal syntax can be used to express <a>lists</a>,\n    by surrounding the list with\n    <span class=\"codepoint\" translate=\"no\"><bdi lang=\"en\">&#x00AB;</bdi>\n    <code class=\"uname\">U+00AB Left-Pointing Double Angle Quotation Mark </code></span>\n    and\n    <span class=\"codepoint\" translate=\"no\"><bdi lang=\"en\">&#x00BB;</bdi>\n    <code class=\"uname\">U+00BB Right-Pointing Double Angle Quotation Mark </code></span>\n    characters, and separating its <a for=list>items</a> with commas. An indexing syntax \n    can be used by providing a zero-based index into a list inside square brackets.\n    The index cannot be out-of-bounds, except when used with <a for=list>exists</a>. \n```\n\nThat renders (approximately, as this lacks the CSS) into the following:\n> <p>For notational convenience, a literal syntax can be used to express <a>lists</a>,\n>     by surrounding the list with\n>     <span class=\"codepoint\" translate=\"no\"><bdi lang=\"en\">&#x00AB;</bdi>\n>     <code class=\"uname\">U+00AB Left-Pointing Double Angle Quotation Mark </code></span>\n>     and\n>     <span class=\"codepoint\" translate=\"no\"><bdi lang=\"en\">&#x00BB;</bdi>\n>     <code class=\"uname\">U+00BB Right-Pointing Double Angle Quotation Mark </code></span>\n>     characters, and separating its <a for=list>items</a> with commas. An indexing syntax \n>     can be used by providing a zero-based index into a list inside square brackets.\n>     The index cannot be out-of-bounds, except when used with <a for=list>exists</a>. </p>",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
